  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/src/operation/area.rs` (`minus_standing`): the result \"enclosed area minus standing part material\" loses each loop whose absolute area is below `ISLAND_AREA_MIN` (1e-4 mm2).\n- `crates/geometry/src/geo2d/slivers.rs`: new method `Region::without_slivers(min_area)`. It filters loops. It does not change a kept loop. A measure that is not positive and finite removes nothing.\n- `crates/geometry/src/geo2d.rs`: one line, `mod slivers;`.\n- `crates/geometry/tests/region_slivers.rs`: two new tests for the method.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/frame_cost_probe.rs`: new pin `area_preview_of_the_default_containment_is_filled`. The helper `adaptive_preview` keeps its behaviour and calls the new `adaptive_preview_with(h, patch, containment)`. The pin selects the welded face with the most strips itself (the concave outer wall of fig8).\n- `docs/decisions/2766-preview-sliver-loops.md`: the decision entry.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe pocket family on a part cuts the enclosed area minus the part material that stands in it. The enclosed area and the part section share a wall. The two tessellations of that wall disagree by about 1 um. The difference then has 3-point loops of 5e-9 to 1.5e-7 mm2. A clockwise loop of that kind stands outside each boundary. `Region::triangles` refuses the whole region with \"hole outside any boundary\". Thus `boundary_viz::preview_fill` gave `None` for the biggest fig8 patch with the default Containment.\n\n`selection_region` gives the same region to generation. Thus the slivers also reached generation. This fix removes them there too.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBoth captures use the same fig8 concave outer-wall patch with default Containment and the Boundary group open.\nThe before capture disables the sliver filter in `minus_standing` to reproduce the missing fill.\nThe after capture uses the restored PR head.\nThe images are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\n| Before: sliver filter disabled | After: sliver filter restored |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Fig8 default Containment before the fix](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/b7993ca26e8fa68ea8ac24238617e5c901dd35c5/2796/before.png) | ![Fig8 default Containment after the fix](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/b7993ca26e8fa68ea8ac24238617e5c901dd35c5/2796/after.png) |\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `egui_app::tests::frame_cost_probe::area_preview_of_the_default_containment_is_filled` (camcraft-ui lib). It asserts that the preview has a fill, that the region has no loop below 1e-4 mm2, and that the fill area is equal to the region area.\n- `without_slivers_drops_near_zero_loops_and_keeps_the_real_ones` and `without_slivers_changes_nothing_for_a_clean_region_or_a_bad_measure` (camcraft-geometry, `region_slivers`).\n\nRed before the fix: yes. On `upstream/main` 971c23faa the UI pin failed at \"the area preview is filled\".\n\nMutations:\n\n- Old `area.rs` from `upstream/main`: the UI pin is red. With the fix again: green. The same check on the final tree (the old line in `minus_standing`): red, then green.\n- `without_slivers` made a no-op: `without_slivers_drops_near_zero_loops_and_keeps_the_real_ones` is red (4 loops, not 2). With the method again: green.\n\nAuthor gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed on head `99a91308f`. The quick tier fell back to batch because geometry changed: 934 steps, 0 failed, 57.5 minutes. An earlier run on head 37d295cf0 was also green (922 steps). The last step is `cargo clippy ... --all-targets -- -D warnings` for geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion, app and ui. It is clean.\n\nThe gate ran with `RUSTC_WRAPPER` empty, because the shared sccache server on this machine did not answer.\n\n## Independent review validation\n\nThe [latest review](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2796#issuecomment-7022512995) tested head `99a91308f54dc67573aebb28e832b2d159fbc061`.\nIt used a clean trial merge of main `e048b103ca649e24048268e1a050f0b4686a997a`.\nNo GitHub runner ran.\n\nThe reviewer ran `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 935 steps, 3 failed steps, 75.6 minutes.\nGeometry caused the batch fallback.\nThe debug build and clippy passed.\nThe preview pin and both `region_slivers` tests passed.\n\nThe failed steps were `ui suites: lib`, `ui suites: egui_app`, and `ui suites: shell`.\nEleven UI tests failed.\nThe report and headless tests could not create a graphics adapter.\nRepeated runs had the same adapter errors or returned exit code 1.\nThis review gate was red.\nRecheck the affected tests on a machine with a graphics adapter before merge.\n\nThe reviewer also checked both mutations.\nRemoving the call in `minus_standing` made the preview pin fail at `the area preview is filled`.\nMaking `without_slivers` return its input made the geometry pin fail with four loops instead of two.\nThe tests passed after each restoration.\n\n## Author-side recheck\n\nRechecked unchanged head `99a91308f54dc67573aebb28e832b2d159fbc061` on Linux with the Vulkan software renderer.\nThe fig8 default-Containment preview pin failed when the sliver filter was removed and passed after it was restored.\nThe before/after screenshots above come from that same fixture.\nAll temporary capture hooks were removed before validation.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 934 steps, 0 failed steps.\nClippy passed with `--all-targets -- -D warnings` for the touched crates.\nThe UI library reported 1260 passed, 0 failed, and 7 ignored tests; all UI integration suites passed.\nThe latest review's red gate remains recorded above as a historical result on its named trial merge.\nThe adapter-dependent paths passed in this recheck.\n\n## Heavy lanes\n\nThe reviewer ran `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` on the restored trial merge.\nThe run completed 217 steps with 0 failed steps in 29.0 minutes.\nThe release build passed in 288 seconds.\nThe reviewer reported 56 passing motion tests and 42 passing app tests.\nThe gate accepted the marked checks that failed as expected.\n\n- `app heavy: adaptive_fig8_crossing`: 2 tests passed.\n- `app heavy: whole_model_pocket`: 1 test passed.\n- `app heavy: shared_face_bodies_finish`: all 6 gouge checks passed.\n\nThese results cover the named trial merge.\nPixel snapshots did not run.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Pixel snapshots.\n- The heavy results above cover the reviewer's named trial merge.\n- No other model is known to have slivers in this difference. The golden suites of the gate show if one has.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- No open PR changes the same function.\n- #2704 and #2767 merged while this work was in progress. #2704 changed `biggest_patch` to a convex bore wall, so the pin no longer uses that helper. The branch has two merges of `upstream/main` (no hand edits in the merges). The second commit adapts the pin.\n- `upstream/main` moved again after the last gate (to e048b103c). The branch merges with it without a conflict.\n\nChangelog: fix: the area preview of a 2D pocket-family operation on a picked part face has a fill again when the region had loops of near-zero area (fig8 patch, default Containment); generation gets the same clean region.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #2766\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
